{"hw":"ἄττα1","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">ἄττα1</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">ἄττα</span> (A), <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Att.</span> </span> for <span class=\"gk\">ἄσσα,</span> (q.v.). <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">II</span> <span class=\"lex-orth gk\">ἅττα</span> for <span class=\"gk\">ἅσσα,</span> = ἅτινα, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.Com.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">49</span> </span>, etc.</div></div><div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">ἄττα2</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">ἄττα</span> (B), a salutation used to elders, <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">father,</b> <span class=\"gk\">ἄττα γεραιέ</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">9.607</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Od.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">16.31</span> </span>, etc.; said to be Thess. by <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Eust.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">777.54</span> </span>. (From child-language.)</div></div>"}